{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:48:56.244582Z","id":"330da47c587f3038db62510f89a7191b58463ed7b68bc6144df800b829cb9554","body":{"detail":"docView keeps id, path, data, version and updated_at, so the daemon's placeholder {doc_id, version, withheld: {authors}} becomes {version} with exists: true, and dbList (plugins/pi/src/clax.ts:1173) never passes withheld_count on. Nothing leaks, but a Pi agent reads Mia's document as empty and its listing as complete, where the Rust tools (crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs doc_view and do_db_list) and clax db say it is withheld and by whom.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":464},"end":{"line":466},"content_hash":"7628b2d8f4308706fedbc0ff68e336d720b50d5273ef1ce11046b7d868512b4c"},"suggested_fix":"Mirror crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs doc_view: a document with withheld becomes {id: doc_id, version, withheld}; copy withheld_count into the listing when present; add a Pi test with a placeholder.","summary":"Pi's db tools show a withheld document as an existing document with only a version, and drop a listing's withheld_count","supersedes":"d3dae369d6ffa5fe97a9665535bc21e467151242f447966d01b324ac20584419","tags":["people","depends:task-19","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:48:56.248118Z","id":"c22449dc493091c626dda06d7530330d53ed27189ebd02876cdcd908e4f659af","body":{"detail":"A version lists no file withheld from the reader (files_withheld counts them), so clax_read of such a path throws not_found \"version N of X has no file '<path>'\". The Rust tools (crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs do_read) instead fetch the bytes when files_withheld > 0 and hand the daemon's 403 withheld answer, which names the authors and never the path (api_mcp::the_read_tool_answers_a_withheld_file_as_withheld). no_canary_reaches_an_agent_through_pi counts the echo as a leak of MIACANARYfilename.html.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":926},"end":{"line":927},"content_hash":"c3e5c7fe256c6b72857954f8c3afeb1c01188a8525431c01f11f9d0c25906cd5"},"summary":"Pi's read tool reports a withheld file as missing and echoes the name it was asked for","supersedes":"5bdd800f71d4cec870762a9efefa98dd85f91037db618235b2fa9b739d5a934e","tags":["visibility","depends:task-19","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/client.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:12:47.262999Z","id":"1420a49a5d91a92e7e1aa8100d7ae5dc8272618f0706e9dae45464f3a196557e","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-08 §6.8: a grant request naming a session without X-Clax-Session-Secret is 401 invalid_session_proof. Pi has no remote mode at this point (plan Task 19 adds it), and local Pi uses the daemon token, which needs no secret. Task 19's remote client must take session_secret from its registration answer, send it on every request naming the session, write <home>/remote-sessions/pi-<harness session ID>.json (0600) as the shim does (clax_core::remote::SessionFiles), treat invalid_session_proof like unknown_session (register again), and remove the file at session end.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":321},"end":{"line":325},"content_hash":"c5e149f6190b9213f5362845bd146d5472da763dff33d4e84efcd2d3356b2f9a"},"summary":"Pi's remote mode must send its session's secret beside X-Clax-Session and keep it on disk for its clax children","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/client.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:20:43.736131Z","id":"1a0c9802ee5ef3d4779cf14569819e3f3d3784c5a6c65f22a9dc897f8bf4af86","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9be93c11","summary":"Pi's remote mode signs every request (plugins/pi/src/remote.ts), takes session_secret from registration, sends X-Clax-Session-Secret beside X-Clax-Session, writes remote-sessions/pi-s-<id>.json 0600 (dir 0700), registers again on invalid_session_proof or unknown_session, and removes the file at session end. Evidence: plugins/pi/test/remote.test.ts 'signs every request, proves its session with its secret, keeps it in its credential file, and registers again when the proof is refused' passes; api_canary::no_canary_reaches_a_persons_agent_through_pi_in_remote_mode drives the real Pi as Sam's agent and passes.","supersedes":"1420a49a5d91a92e7e1aa8100d7ae5dc8272618f0706e9dae45464f3a196557e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:20:43.739729Z","id":"e57123c13178c291a3897dbec4469a0ebee5b73bbfe1ddc1c92024db9bed9fc1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9be93c11","summary":"Pi's read fetches the bytes when files_withheld > 0 and hands the daemon's 403 withheld answer, as crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs do_read does. Evidence: api_canary::no_canary_reaches_an_agent_through_pi (real Pi in RPC mode) passes; with the fetch removed it reports 'leaked MIACANARYfilename.html' and 'MIACANARYcarried.css'.","supersedes":"602b52bc0e7c50a092999bdee0cd1c9be8f7cbe70ec8d673d05457d4c73a3241","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:20:43.740568Z","id":"3f7eda6619dce9beb7a2229e05bffb8bb2df0b9876fab08f80b9fb2756df7ae9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9be93c11","summary":"handoverOf keeps withheld; handedOver counts it; results carry withheld and notes as the Rust render does; wait_for_feedback's call_again is false when placeholders arrive. Evidence: plugins/pi/test/clax.test.ts 'withheld placeholders alone count as handed over' passes; the read echo is closed with 602b52bc.","supersedes":"6ec316978fc87509b44ef951dd8d4c8613116be6adcd7e30f21ee2c0e30d6821","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:20:43.741416Z","id":"b8329d7f99736c5a543ec0d5222c51f8d6777bfae41e9465056407ed71d60363","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9be93c11","summary":"docView mirrors doc_view (a withheld document is {id: doc_id, version, withheld}) and db_list passes withheld_count on. Evidence: plugins/pi/test/remote.test.ts 'the db tools show a withheld document as withheld ...' passes, and api_canary::no_canary_reaches_a_persons_agent_through_pi_in_remote_mode sees withheld_count 2 for Mia's documents.","supersedes":"a37fe1ccd67c67e5ba49647f223686d24807edafd952e711ac7964eaf4f9fae8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/client.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:20:43.742259Z","id":"a13bdc6cbab35a978d06cc0646e6102639ea182d9d4e70733b19a84600610f2a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9be93c11","summary":"Pi's registration carries repo and branch from repoAndBranch (plugins/pi/src/git.ts, no git process, as clax_core::names::repo_and_branch). Evidence: plugins/pi/test/clax.test.ts 'registers with the repository and branch of its working directory, which name the agent' (name chart-repo-axis) and remote.test.ts 'reads the repository and branch from the files' pass.","supersedes":"30ef13bd774b557a1ff03179e1f5538575641fc61325026d493b8b893b52fd06","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/remote.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:20:43.744932Z","id":"e188ad6f43d6776280e7641753961434c137ab316ab3f45c2c8c3b22abbc1a04","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-08 §6.8 opens every credential file through the directory's own handle (openat with O_NOFOLLOW), as clax_core::remote::SessionFiles does. Node has no openat, so SessionFiles here lstats <home>/remote-sessions and then opens <dir>/<name> with O_NOFOLLOW on the last component only. Another process of the same OS user could race a symlink in for the directory; that user can already read the machine's key (§6.8's trust limit), so this stops no attacker the Rust client stops, but it is weaker than the spec's wording.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":214},"end":{"line":298},"content_hash":"a758379c62d93f046a2f1ca484e5bb5a7e1d760a2a3335042e964175402e0b5b"},"suggested_fix":"Open the directory with fs.opendirSync and compare its dev/ino before and after each file open, or keep the file I/O in a `clax` subcommand.","summary":"Pi's credential files check the directory with lstat, then open the file by path with O_NOFOLLOW: a directory swapped for a symbolic link between the two is followed","tags":["security","remote","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/client.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:20:43.745014Z","id":"41fdb3011b477eeb4e9bc44a85f0e8c5df84e148c0d565512a1e9ebfdc59674a","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-08 §6.8 names a row with a parent PID also <harness>-p-<parent PID>.json, written only when the parent's start time can be told. The extension cannot read a process's start time without a child process, so it writes no such file; a client that knows Pi's process but not its session ID finds no credential. No client does so today (Codex's shim is the only parent-PID reader).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":323},"end":{"line":326},"content_hash":"413c6068cf75a3a7ecab204dc282c96261df3978b01faee6d7443dcd828961af"},"summary":"Pi writes its session's credential under its harness session ID only, never a parent-PID file","tags":["remote","revisit:a client looks up Pi's credential by parent PID","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/client.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:02:04.320031Z","id":"7f08d82ba2b150473775f44fab732e432b7f1f9627f183fe1172ef46ae1e8fd4","body":{"detail":"Mutation: `backoffs < BACKOFF_S.length` replaced by an unbounded retry; `npx vitest run` in plugins/pi passed 100/100. The Rust client's equivalent (crates/clax-core/src/remote.rs:1311-1345) is tested at remote.rs:1600. Each retry also reuses the timeout computed before the first attempt, so a retried request can run up to four timeouts plus about 9 s past its deadline. Both clients also retry the semantic 429 limit_reached of an approval ask (the person holds 100 open requests) three times, about 7-9 s, before the agent sees it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":170},"end":{"line":195},"content_hash":"fb9be7847eb6aa0a0dd52a1600e33413696f7ee1b00d9e54f9dc7d16b1e5285e"},"suggested_fix":"Add a remote.test.ts case with a server answering 503 busy four times and 401 stale_request with a Date header; bound the retries by the request's deadline.","summary":"Pi's stale_request and limit_reached/busy retries have no test: a mutant that retries busy forever passes all 100 Pi tests","tags":["review","remote","tests","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/remote.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:02:04.320183Z","id":"209ff5828601fff2d3d2ea40532f9f1e6404c1c1938207eda9f74355772c3cf6","body":{"detail":"Swapping <home>/remote-sessions for a symbolic link between lstat and open needs write access to <home> as the same OS user, who can already read remote.key and every credential file (spec 2026-10-08 §21: the machine's OS user is the boundary). Node has no openat; /dev/fd/<n>/<name> does not resolve through a directory descriptor on macOS, and a dev/ino recheck after open narrows the window without closing it. Proposed: §6.8 says a client without openat (Pi) lstats the directory and opens each file with O_NOFOLLOW, and this record becomes a waiver. Owner's decision.","kind":"comment","references":"e188ad6f43d6776280e7641753961434c137ab316ab3f45c2c8c3b22abbc1a04","span":{"start":{"line":214},"end":{"line":298},"content_hash":"a758379c62d93f046a2f1ca484e5bb5a7e1d760a2a3335042e964175402e0b5b"},"summary":"Risk judged nil beyond §6.8's trust limit; the spec should name Pi's weaker form rather than Pi growing a workaround","tags":["review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/remote.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:02:04.320283Z","id":"eeb6470bfae8122da316feb4f477ee2692838dbc028f4cc7f44dd05a75e4ec8f","body":{"detail":"SessionFiles.write above unlinks the temporary file on a failed write; storeClip unlinks only on a failed rename. A full disk leaves one .<aid>-<tid>.<hex>.tmp per failed fetch in remote-cache/clips.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":381},"end":{"line":403},"content_hash":"c417c23ae068402dd3355ecff1448c95a971003060d94f19f824123f9bda14e3"},"summary":"storeClip leaves its .tmp file behind when the write or fsync fails (the finally closes the descriptor but never unlinks)","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/client.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:55:01.461192Z","id":"997379faeb3ec88317a4f5ace18bfe351bd4d46e7432f2d1366f574aad38c649","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7a06e2cd","summary":"Evidence: plugins/pi/test/remote.test.ts 'retries busy and limit_reached three times, after 1, 2 and 4 s with up to a quarter more, then gives up' and 'retries a stale request once, with the daemon's clock, and only once' pass with an injected sleep (Remote.sleep); unbounded retries fail the first (M2 killed). The byte-length nit: 'counts an agent header's bytes, not its UTF-16 units' kills M1.","supersedes":"7f08d82ba2b150473775f44fab732e432b7f1f9627f183fe1172ef46ae1e8fd4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/remote.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:55:01.463558Z","id":"8068d86b6eb9ac92ed1feb4b0f31a8dd086ba4cd98df7f906ead5ff36a9ccf52","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7a06e2cd","summary":"storeClip now closes and unlinks its temporary file when the write or fsync fails (7a06e2cd).","supersedes":"eeb6470bfae8122da316feb4f477ee2692838dbc028f4cc7f44dd05a75e4ec8f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/remote.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:55:01.467344Z","id":"87716da25029c7af75789472f5734fbf4d09e04a53d841f2ae6385f9dbc1cbc3","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e188ad6f43d6776280e7641753961434c137ab316ab3f45c2c8c3b22abbc1a04","summary":"Coordinator ruling (Task 19 fix round 1): Pi keeps its lstat-then-O_NOFOLLOW form; spec §6.8 now names it (7a06e2cd), with the reasoning that only a process of the same OS user can swap the directory, and that user can already read remote.key and every credential file (the trust limit). Whether this record becomes a waiver is the owner's call.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:16:36.717542Z","id":"a0137115252e6133676270486e8ecece4801933b5156138f42cd32b6954c227d","body":{"detail":"When AbortSignal.timeout fires during a backoff of 4 s (plus up to a quarter more), the sleep finishes before the next attempt fails on the aborted signal, so one fetch can take about 9 s against a CLIP_FETCH_MS of 5 s. The ensure before the request (DaemonClient.request) is not bounded by the signal either.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":844},"end":{"line":844},"content_hash":"cada5a2288be6ae437854cf35bfcf6a1a4db2907254bcbac2644febc8e51086b"},"suggested_fix":"Race the backoff sleep against opts.signal in sendRemote.","summary":"A Pi clip fetch can run past CLIP_FETCH_MS: the busy/limit_reached backoff in sendRemote (plugins/pi/src/client.ts:202) is not cut short by the fetch's AbortSignal","tags":["review","remote","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/client.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T22:16:49.647954Z","id":"9837c17228af828f62318e51c246c0cc23be3d42f85f93e7eb1b5a188ca24920","body":{"detail":"The Rust CLI and shim read at most clax_core::remote::MAX_RESPONSE_BYTES of a remote answer (crates/clax-cli/src/remote.rs capped_body; crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs:1647-1665) and turn a Date beyond MAX_OFFSET_S into a clock_skew refusal with clock_skew_message. sendRemote applies maxBytes only where a caller passes it (clips), and when learnOffset refuses an offset beyond MAX_OFFSET_S it returns the stale_request response as is, so the person never reads that their clocks differ.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":183},"end":{"line":206},"content_hash":"083f2dd18f916d2b4c619f2103ada7272bd5e731ec7d99fdcb53819c1f0f4bd3"},"suggested_fix":"Give sendRemote a default maxBytes of 128 MiB and map a refused offset to clock_skew with the same wording as clock_skew_message.","summary":"Pi's remote client reads answers uncapped and answers a too-far Date with the raw stale_request, unlike the Rust clients","tags":["review","remote","pi","final-review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/client.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T01:10:27.150228Z","id":"a82b2014680056b78108a104dd7d5496a24a63a1f91dbd45e19a2291fab197e9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c5f95b5b","summary":"Fixed in c5f95b5b: sendRemote caps every answer at MAX_RESPONSE_BYTES and answers a stale_request whose Date is beyond MAX_OFFSET_S with 401 clock_skew and the Rust clock_skew_message. Evidence: plugins/pi npx vitest run test/remote.test.ts -> 14 passed, including 'says the clocks differ...' and 'reads at most MAX_RESPONSE_BYTES...'.","supersedes":"9837c17228af828f62318e51c246c0cc23be3d42f85f93e7eb1b5a188ca24920","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"25a883baadbec89e717d639c4fe8f14c92312f886458ef3992c71a49f347cbed","body":{"detail":"handoverOf keeps feedback, answers and text; a poll that hands over only placeholders (spec §8.3: N comments from <name> ... are withheld) has empty feedback, so Pi's piggyback and wait_for_feedback treat it as nothing handed over and drop the text, and wait_for_feedback says call_again. The injection loop sends res.text and so carries them. The MCP shim's Handover (crates/clax-mcp/src/render.rs) counts withheld. Pi's sweep (api_canary::no_canary_reaches_an_agent_through_pi) also still reports one leak: an error echoing a path the call named, 'version 1 of <id> has no file MIACANARYfilename.html'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":297},"end":{"line":297},"content_hash":"f537bc15e77c9dfe41600cf783ff302b8ddbd572a675a9437d7b88482c530940"},"summary":"Pi's tool-result handover ignores the feedback poll's withheld placeholders","supersedes":"54d36fd799b194dd4934a9e3226a6d31af59670de17a334b9635dd8ac78d5d00","tags":["people","depends:task-19","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"8351d02bfca12b3c5a8d36914a8dc8dceabe99deee3d3a5f58fc616d82e8dbff","body":{"detail":"docView keeps id, path, data, version and updated_at, so the daemon's placeholder {doc_id, version, withheld: {authors}} becomes {version} with exists: true, and dbList (plugins/pi/src/clax.ts:1173) never passes withheld_count on. Nothing leaks, but a Pi agent reads Mia's document as empty and its listing as complete, where the Rust tools (crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs doc_view and do_db_list) and clax db say it is withheld and by whom.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":469},"end":{"line":471},"content_hash":"7628b2d8f4308706fedbc0ff68e336d720b50d5273ef1ce11046b7d868512b4c"},"suggested_fix":"Mirror crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs doc_view: a document with withheld becomes {id: doc_id, version, withheld}; copy withheld_count into the listing when present; add a Pi test with a placeholder.","summary":"Pi's db tools show a withheld document as an existing document with only a version, and drop a listing's withheld_count","supersedes":"0aac7fd0307f42d8ea49d5941659790327b5920a4d9ac07bfb811a38ebb57cb8","tags":["people","depends:task-19","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"19db2cd25596feb09bf5b442999c9cc18c1a87970709f5759992a9fbd61dc095","body":{"detail":"A version lists no file withheld from the reader (files_withheld counts them), so clax_read of such a path throws not_found \"version N of X has no file '<path>'\". The Rust tools (crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs do_read) instead fetch the bytes when files_withheld > 0 and hand the daemon's 403 withheld answer, which names the authors and never the path (api_mcp::the_read_tool_answers_a_withheld_file_as_withheld). no_canary_reaches_an_agent_through_pi counts the echo as a leak of MIACANARYfilename.html.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":931},"end":{"line":932},"content_hash":"c3e5c7fe256c6b72857954f8c3afeb1c01188a8525431c01f11f9d0c25906cd5"},"summary":"Pi's read tool reports a withheld file as missing and echoes the name it was asked for","supersedes":"25172a75e09f2eb991a221a876d242c2e8ddeef6877c6e6b6e389f170f1e0dcf","tags":["visibility","depends:task-19","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:31:12.201709Z","id":"61bcce62d45483b82ed9b527c2d92d2560d1994ad1df43d1f90dda36e0273c7a","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate head left by a merge: the same record as 54d36fd799b194dd4934a9e3226a6d31af59670de17a334b9635dd8ac78d5d00 (kept), re-anchored on a parallel branch.","supersedes":"829f7340f43588113c9cf75448191e8a68a5657eee2c457b6ae5757cf3b7815e","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:31:12.209418Z","id":"75ce4f7063a759b6c9885c3e3de1914f1066f79b2d4e10ac2532e39b80b08eb2","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate head left by a merge: the same record as 0aac7fd0307f42d8ea49d5941659790327b5920a4d9ac07bfb811a38ebb57cb8 (kept), re-anchored on a parallel branch.","supersedes":"330da47c587f3038db62510f89a7191b58463ed7b68bc6144df800b829cb9554","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:31:12.217068Z","id":"5451b7094a4e8fb7d93d41f1632245a564740b72b157bbe1f437e7baacd65391","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate head left by a merge: the same record as 25172a75e09f2eb991a221a876d242c2e8ddeef6877c6e6b6e389f170f1e0dcf (kept), re-anchored on a parallel branch.","supersedes":"c22449dc493091c626dda06d7530330d53ed27189ebd02876cdcd908e4f659af","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:23.070490Z","id":"66a3a02bde75b7d1c2cbcab38d8c929e5589031106483e166a5108b269c032d6","body":{"detail":"handoverOf keeps feedback, answers and text; a poll that hands over only placeholders (spec §8.3: N comments from <name> ... are withheld) has empty feedback, so Pi's piggyback and wait_for_feedback treat it as nothing handed over and drop the text, and wait_for_feedback says call_again. The injection loop sends res.text and so carries them. The MCP shim's Handover (crates/clax-mcp/src/render.rs) counts withheld. Pi's sweep (api_canary::no_canary_reaches_an_agent_through_pi) also still reports one leak: an error echoing a path the call named, 'version 1 of <id> has no file MIACANARYfilename.html'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":347},"end":{"line":347},"content_hash":"f537bc15e77c9dfe41600cf783ff302b8ddbd572a675a9437d7b88482c530940"},"summary":"Pi's tool-result handover ignores the feedback poll's withheld placeholders","supersedes":"25a883baadbec89e717d639c4fe8f14c92312f886458ef3992c71a49f347cbed","tags":["people","depends:task-19","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:23.084021Z","id":"824fff2198c660900402911cc722ef7d4fd149a1aeffe7f25fcd728badb3410c","body":{"detail":"When AbortSignal.timeout fires during a backoff of 4 s (plus up to a quarter more), the sleep finishes before the next attempt fails on the aborted signal, so one fetch can take about 9 s against a CLIP_FETCH_MS of 5 s. The ensure before the request (DaemonClient.request) is not bounded by the signal either.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":874},"end":{"line":874},"content_hash":"cada5a2288be6ae437854cf35bfcf6a1a4db2907254bcbac2644febc8e51086b"},"suggested_fix":"Race the backoff sleep against opts.signal in sendRemote.","summary":"A Pi clip fetch can run past CLIP_FETCH_MS: the busy/limit_reached backoff in sendRemote (plugins/pi/src/client.ts:202) is not cut short by the fetch's AbortSignal","supersedes":"a0137115252e6133676270486e8ecece4801933b5156138f42cd32b6954c227d","tags":["review","remote","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/client.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:23.097795Z","id":"e9cd3554b5f462254b316d1eb9eb99377a82817ab87fbf1588d94404f59d1d1b","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-08 §6.8 names a row with a parent PID also <harness>-p-<parent PID>.json, written only when the parent's start time can be told. The extension cannot read a process's start time without a child process, so it writes no such file; a client that knows Pi's process but not its session ID finds no credential. No client does so today (Codex's shim is the only parent-PID reader).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":341},"end":{"line":344},"content_hash":"413c6068cf75a3a7ecab204dc282c96261df3978b01faee6d7443dcd828961af"},"summary":"Pi writes its session's credential under its harness session ID only, never a parent-PID file","supersedes":"41fdb3011b477eeb4e9bc44a85f0e8c5df84e148c0d565512a1e9ebfdc59674a","tags":["remote","revisit:a client looks up Pi's credential by parent PID","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:53:20.511589Z","id":"d4e02df474186674d39771f5fb39422faba7ec595922553ef8e7c3648c2d560d","body":{"detail":"The input handler records terminal activity for every Pi input whose source is not \"extension\" (Pi 0.73.1 InputSource is \"interactive\" | \"rpc\" | \"extension\"; AgentSession.sendUserMessage, which the Clax delivery loop at plugins/pi/src/clax.ts:1822 calls, prompts with source \"extension\"). An \"rpc\" prompt is counted because RPC frontends (an editor driving Pi) relay what the person typed. A program driving Pi over RPC with no person behind it would then read as the person being at the terminal.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1900},"end":{"line":1906},"content_hash":"0b019290b541d0c2112b63c908f357afe716b915126dd988fb5884b57bd71aef"},"summary":"Count only source \"interactive\" input as a typed prompt, not \"rpc\" as well","tags":["revisit:Pi is driven over RPC by a program that sends prompts no person typed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:03:15.439668Z","id":"17fdfeca9ec6807a6d41d2aa95812ceb19eb55247ebe787d498f22061eeb161b","body":{"detail":"The input handler records terminal activity for every Pi input whose source is not \"extension\" (Pi 0.73.1 InputSource is \"interactive\" | \"rpc\" | \"extension\"; AgentSession.sendUserMessage, which the Clax delivery loop at plugins/pi/src/clax.ts:1822 calls, prompts with source \"extension\"). An \"rpc\" prompt is counted because RPC frontends (an editor driving Pi) relay what the person typed. A program driving Pi over RPC with no person behind it would then read as the person being at the terminal.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1901},"end":{"line":1907},"content_hash":"0b019290b541d0c2112b63c908f357afe716b915126dd988fb5884b57bd71aef"},"summary":"Count only source \"interactive\" input as a typed prompt, not \"rpc\" as well","supersedes":"d4e02df474186674d39771f5fb39422faba7ec595922553ef8e7c3648c2d560d","tags":["revisit:Pi is driven over RPC by a program that sends prompts no person typed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
